<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Robert Kocharyan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1954">1954</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Robert Kocharyan is an Armenian politician who led the self-proclaimed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nagorno-karabakh">Nagorno-Karabakh</a> Republic and then served as president of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a> from 1998 to 2008. He came to power after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/levon-ter-petrosyan">Levon Ter-Petrosyan</a>'s resignation and kept close ties with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>. In March 2008 clashes between police and protesters disputing the election of his successor, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serzh-sargsyan">Serzh Sargsyan</a>, left ten people dead.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/robert-kocharyan.jpg" alt="Robert Kocharyan" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hasmiktergulanyan12 · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Khocharyan12.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
